        nail discoloration), classified under B35.1 (tinea unguium). No SNOMED CT concept exists for this
        specific presentation. SNOMED CT has 4006158 (111202002) but that is a nail-finding morphology
        concept, not a dermatophyte infection. The best defensible standard concept is SNOMED CT 40515068
        (30757001) which fully subsumes the source as a clinical entity (the source is a trichophyton
        nail infection, i.e. a tinea unguium). Broader: target subsumes the source. Low tier: clinical
        breadth mismatch (the source's leukonychia-trichophytica morphology is lost), no separate
        crosswalk.
